        "underTheHood": "When `con.prepareStatement(sql)` is called, the database parses, compiles, and optimizes the execution plan. When `executeQuery()` runs, parameter values are transmitted via binary protocol packets separate from the statement text. The database engine never re-parses the statement, making SQL injection impossible.",
